<+># Anti-Pattern Sentinel — Registry (machine-readable)\n# Canonical source: django-expertise spec §2.1 and §7.\n# severity: error = must fix before accept; warning = review / justify.\n# detection types: ast (python AST), regex, template-pattern, heuristic, manual.\n\nmeta:\n  name: anti-pattern-sentinel\n  version: 1.0.0\n  spec: django-expertise-spec §2.1 / §7\n  file_types: [py, html, htm, js]\n\nanti_patterns:\n\n  - id: A-001\n    name: Signals for Business Logic\n    why_wrong: >\n      Hidden side effects, hard to debug, breaks the explicit request/response\n      flow. Signals are framework-level hooks, not business logic carriers.\n    django_way: >\n      Explicit service-layer calls in views/forms; use signals only for\n      framework-level instrumentation (audit, request lifecycle).\n    ref: https://docs.djangoproject.com/en/stable/topics/signals/\n    severity: error\n    detectors:\n      - type: ast\n        hint: FunctionDef/AsyncFunctionDef decorated with @receiver(post_save|pre_save|pre_delete|post_delete|m2m_changed, ...) in app code.\n        implemented: true\n      - type: ast\n        hint: Call to `<Signal>.connect(...)` where signal is post_save/pre_save/pre_delete/post_delete/m2m_changed.\n        implemented: true\n\n  - id: A-002\n    name: Custom User Model Without Need\n    why_wrong: Unnecessary migration complexity; AbstractBaseUser reimplements auth plumbing Django already provides.\n    django_way: Extend AbstractUser, add a OneToOne Profile model, or use a JSONField on the profile.\n    ref: https://docs.djangoproject.com/en/stable/topics/auth/customizing/\n    severity: warning\n    detectors:\n      - type: ast\n        hint: ClassDef subclassing AbstractBaseUser without a docstring or comment justifying the full custom user.\n        implemented: true\n\n  - id: A-003\n    name: N+1 Queries in Templates\n    why_wrong: Each loop iteration hits the database for related objects (e.g. {{ product.category.name }}).\n    django_way: Use select_related()/prefetch_related() in the View queryset.\n    ref: https://docs.djangoproject.com/en/stable/ref/models/querysets/#prefetch-related\n    severity: warning\n    detectors:\n      - type: heuristic\n        hint: >\n          Template `{% for x in <var> %}` where `<var>` is a queryset context variable,\n          combined with a chain access `{{ item.<rel>.<attr> }}` inside the loop, while\n          the corresponding view file (views.py in the scanned tree) shows no\n          select_related/prefetch_related for that variable.\n        implemented: true\n\n  - id: A-004\n    name: Business Logic in Templates\n    why_wrong: Templates should be presentation-only; complex {% if %} chains and DB work in template tags are untestable.\n    django_way: Model methods, Manager methods, or View-computed context.\n    ref: https://docs.djangoproject.com/en/stable/ref/templates/language/\n    severity: error\n    detectors:\n      - type: regex\n        hint: ORM calls (`.objects.`, `.filter(`, `.get(` on models) inside templatetags/*.py files, especially in @register.simple_tag functions.\n        implemented: true\n      - type: template-pattern\n        hint: More than 3 nested {% if %} levels in a template (if-chain complexity heuristic).\n        implemented: true\n\n  - id: A-005\n    name: Reinventing the Admin\n    why_wrong: Wasted effort building CRUD/dashboards the admin already handles.\n    django_way: Customize ModelAdmin (list_display, inlines, actions) or use django-jazzmin / django-admin-interface.\n    ref: https://django-jazzmin.readthedocs.io/\n    severity: warning\n    detectors:\n      - type: manual\n        hint: >\n          Manual review. Heuristics (custom 'dashboard' views duplicating ModelAdmin CRUD)\n          produce too many false positives; reviewer should check whether admin customization\n          was considered before hand-rolled CRUD.\n        implemented: false\n\n  - id: A-006\n    name: Raw SQL Without ORM Fallback\n    why_wrong: Loses Django's query optimization and SQL-injection protection.\n    django_way: Use the ORM; raw SQL only for complex reports, with params and a justification comment.\n    ref: https://docs.djangoproject.com/en/stable/topics/db/sql/\n    severity: warning\n    detectors:\n      - type: ast\n        hint: Call `<manager>.raw(...)` or `cursor.execute(...)` / `connection.cursor()` usage.\n        implemented: true\n\n  - id: A-007\n    name: Putting All Logic in Views\n    why_wrong: Views become bloated and untestable; business rules belong in models/services.\n    django_way: Service-layer pattern, model methods, Manager methods; views only orchestrate request/response.\n    ref: https://docs.djangoproject.com/en/stable/topics/class-based-views/intro/\n    severity: warning\n    detectors:\n      - type: heuristic\n        hint: View function body exceeding ~40 non-blank, non-comment lines while performing model mutation directly (status flips + .save() inline).\n        implemented: false\n      - type: manual\n        hint: Manual review of view size and responsibility split.\n        implemented: false\n\n  - id: A-008\n    name: Using Signals for Cache Invalidation\n    why_wrong: Race conditions and unclear flow; cache invalidation via post_save hides when caches are actually refreshed.\n    django_way: Explicit cache calls in save() overrides or in the service layer.\n    ref: https://docs.djangoproject.com/en/stable/topics/cache/\n    severity: warning\n    detectors:\n      - type: ast\n        hint: \"@receiver(post_save|post_delete) whose function body calls cache.delete/cache.set/cache.clear (sub-case of A-001, flagged separately).\"\n        implemented: true\n      - type: manual\n        hint: Manual review of implicit cache invalidation flows.\n        implemented: false\n\n  - id: A-009\n    name: Client-Side Routing for Internal Apps\n    why_wrong: Unnecessary complexity; breaks Django's URL resolver, template rendering and auth/session integration.\n    django_way: hx-boost + server-side routing; HTMX/Hyperscript only, no React/Vue/Angular.\n    ref: https://htmx.org/attributes/hx-boost/\n    severity: error\n    detectors:\n      - type: regex\n        hint: >\n          <script src> tags or import statements referencing react, react-dom, vue,\n          angular, next, nuxt, svelte in .html/.js files.\n        implemented: true\n\n  - id: A-010\n    name: JSON API for HTMX Endpoints\n    why_wrong: HTMX expects HTML fragments, not JSON; a JSON API duplicates the view layer.\n    django_way: Return partial templates from Views (render(request, '_partial.html', ...)).\n    ref: https://htmx.org/\n    severity: warning\n    detectors:\n      - type: heuristic\n        hint: JsonResponse returned from a view function whose name or module path suggests htmx usage (name contains htmx/hx/partial, or sibling templates use hx-* attributes).\n        implemented: true\n\n  - id: A-011\n    name: State in hx-vals or Data Attributes\n    why_wrong: Client-held state is fragile, hard to sync, and a security risk (tamperable).\n    django_way: Server-side state in database or session; hx-vals only for transient UI hints.\n    ref: https://htmx.org/attributes/hx-vals/\n    severity: warning\n    detectors:\n      - type: template-pattern\n        hint: hx-vals containing sensitive-looking keys (user_id, role, price, permission, is_admin) or data-* attributes carrying business state.\n        implemented: false\n      - type: manual\n        hint: Manual review of what state is pushed to the client.\n        implemented: false\n\n  - id: A-012\n    name: Inline Styles for HTMX Indicators\n    why_wrong: Inline style= on indicator elements is inconsistent and hard to maintain.\n    django_way: CSS classes + the htmx-indicator class / hx-indicator attribute pattern.\n    ref: https://htmx.org/attributes/hx-indicator/\n    severity: error\n    detectors:\n      - type: regex\n        hint: Element carrying class*=\"htmx-indicator\" (or id referenced by hx-indicator) that also has an inline style= attribute.\n        implemented: true\n\n  - id: A-013\n    name: Missing Graceful Degradation\n    why_wrong: If the HTMX request fails or JS is disabled, partial-only views break the app.\n    django_way: Views check request.headers.get('HX-Request') and serve both full and partial templates.\n    ref: https://docs.djangoproject.com/en/stable/topics/http/shortcuts/#render\n    severity: error\n    detectors:\n      - type: ast\n        hint: View function that renders a partial template (filename starting with '_') but whose body never checks HX-Request / request.htmx.\n        implemented: true\n\n  - id: A-014\n    name: Over-Prefetching\n    why_wrong: prefetch_related/select_related on relations the template never uses causes memory bloat and slow queries.\n    django_way: Prefetch only what the template actually renders.\n    ref: https://docs.djangoproject.com/en/stable/ref/models/querysets/#prefetch-related\n    severity: warning\n    detectors:\n      - type: manual\n        hint: >\n          Manual review. Cross-referencing prefetched relations with template attribute\n          access requires full context resolution; reviewer checks each prefetch against\n          template usage.\n        implemented: false\n\n  - id: A-015\n    name: Using GenericForeignKey\n    why_wrong: Performance cost (extra joins, no DB-level integrity) and complexity; rarely the right tool.\n    django_way: Concrete model inheritance, explicit FKs, or a JSONField for flexible payloads.\n    ref: https://docs.djangoproject.com/en/stable/ref/contrib/contenttypes/\n    severity: warning\n    detectors:\n      - type: ast\n        hint: Assignment of GenericForeignKey(...) in a model class body.\n        implemented: true\n      - type: regex\n        hint: Import or usage of GenericForeignKey / GenericRelation from django.contrib.contenttypes.\n        implemented: true\n\nmanual_review:\n  A-005: Check whether admin customization (ModelAdmin, jazzmin) was considered before hand-rolled CRUD.\n  A-007: Review view size/responsibility split; business rules belong in models or a service layer.\n  A-011: Review what state is pushed to the client via hx-vals / data-* attributes.\n  A-014: Cross-check each prefetch_related/select_related against actual template usage.\n
